v1.0.54 build 57: Modal scroll perf — wrap modal body ListView in RepaintBoundary, drop BoxShadow on DraggableSheetContainer

Both changes reduce GPU rasterization cost on real device during modal scroll:
- BoxShadow on full-height sheet (height 85% of screen) = saveLayer pass every repaint.
  Without shadow, sheet background paints without offscreen buffer.
- ListView wrapped in RepaintBoundary = list scrolls within own compositing layer,
  doesn't invalidate nav bar / sheet background layer.

Emulator x64 qemu benchmark (no GPU acceleration):
- Modal scroll (50 rapid swipes): avg 3.9-5.3ms = 190-260 FPS, max 12ms
- Modal scroll + picker open: avg 9.9-10.9ms = 90-100 FPS, max 29ms
- Picker wheel scroll (50 flicks): avg 3.5-5.7ms = 175-280 FPS, max 27ms

No perceptible improvement on emulator (already at 200+ FPS), but real device
should benefit since GPU vsync caps at 60 FPS and these optimizations reduce
work-per-frame to give GPU more headroom.
